@petebacondarwin Thanks for the fix. I have good news and bad news. Will start with the good 🚀 

**Good**) Your fix (landed in master & 8.1.x branch) fixed the issue observed for all of the angular bundles. The ivy-ngcc generated file `node_modules/@angular/cdk/bundles/cdk-a11y.umd.js` file now has:
```
    /** @nocollapse */ AriaDescriber.ngInjectableDef = core.ɵɵdefineInjectable({ factory: function AriaDescriber_Factory() { return new AriaDescriber(core.ɵɵinject(common.DOCUMENT)); }, token: AriaDescriber, providedIn: "root" });
AriaDescriber.ngInjectableDef = ɵngcc0.ɵɵdefineInjectable({ token: AriaDescriber, factory: function AriaDescriber_Factory(t) { return new (t || AriaDescriber)(ɵngcc0.ɵɵinject(common.DOCUMENT)); }, providedIn: 'root' });
/*@__PURE__*/ ɵngcc0.ɵsetClassMetadata(AriaDescriber, [{
        type: core.Injectable,
        args: [{ providedIn: 'root' }]
    }], function () { return [{ type: undefined, decorators: [{
                type: core.Inject,
                args: [common.DOCUMENT]
            }] }]; }, { _document: [], describe: [], removeDescription: [], ngOnDestroy: [], _createMessageElement: [], _deleteMessageElement: [], _createMessagesContainer: [], _deleteMessagesContainer: [], _removeCdkDescribedByReferenceIds: [], _addMessageReference: [], _removeMessageReference: [], _isElementDescribedByMessage: [], _canBeDescribed: [], _isElementNode: [] });
    return AriaDescriber;
```

which correctly has `type: core.Injectable,`

**Bad**) The @ngrx umd bundles (from latest 8.1.0 release) still have the same error originally observed in the angular bundles

```
        ActionsSubject = tslib_1.__decorate([
            core.Injectable(),
            tslib_1.__metadata("design:paramtypes", [])
        ], ActionsSubject);
        return ActionsSubject;
```

in `node_modules/@ngrx/store/bundles/store.umd.js.__ivy_ngcc_bak` is transformed to

```
ActionsSubject.ngInjectableDef = ɵngcc0.ɵɵdefineInjectable({ token: ActionsSubject, factory: function ActionsSubject_Factory(t) { return new (t || ActionsSubject)(); }, providedIn: null });
/*@__PURE__*/ ɵngcc0.ɵsetClassMetadata(ActionsSubject, [{
        type: Injectable
    }], function () { return []; }, { next: [], complete: [], ngOnDestroy: [] });
        return ActionsSubject;
```

in `node_modules/@ngrx/store/bundles/store.umd.js` which has `type: Injectable` again and it fails in the browser at runtime.

There is a slight difference in that the ngrx bundle, which has `core.Injectable(),` while the issue observed with the cdk bundle `node_modules/@angular/cdk/bundles/cdk-a11y.umd.js.__ivy_ngcc_bak` had `type: core.Injectable,`.
